# The papers themselves: ~1.1 GB of scans. A GitHub Pages site is capped at
# 1 GB, so the PDFs stay local and the site links to the original hosts.
# Run `python3 scripts/aggregate.py all` to rebuild them from links.tsv.
docs/assets/**/*.pdf

# Raw MarkItDown output — large, mostly watermark noise, and regenerable.
# The cleaned English text (markdown-english/) IS committed and published.
docs/assets/markdown/

# Crawl page cache (regenerable); links.tsv + manifest.json ARE committed,
# because they are what makes the corpus reproducible.
docs/assets/.aggregate/pages/
docs/assets/.aggregate/ocrtmp/
docs/assets/.aggregate/*.tmp

.DS_Store
__pycache__/

# Node / build artifacts
web/node_modules/
web/dist/
*.log

# Compiled Go binary (build with `go build ./cmd/publish`)
/publish
web/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

# Intermediate JSON for the dataset build. The site reads the Parquet, and both
# JSON and Parquet are published to object storage, so the repo keeps the small
# columnar files and not the 6 MB of JSON.
docs/data/questions.json
docs/data/papers.json
